For safe-linking in tcache, the key depends on the chunk's address itself—specifically the upper bits. Two chunks at different heap locations will have different keys, so even if they're the first entry in their respective tcache operations, their encoded values differ. The only scenario where keys match is if chunks occupy the same 4KB page region, which is unlikely given how heap allocations grow sequentially.

